# PLAYER ('@') — the adventurer, top-down, FRONT=UP. The most-seen sprite in the game:
# the BLUE cloak is the only blue in the world. CLOAK rule (learned): wide at the BOTTOM,
# contained A-line — a big back-fan reads like rising out of the ground. ARMS attached and
# in BODY SCALE: they emerge from under the pauldrons, hands visible — shield strapped on
# the left forearm, the sword drawn from the right hand. Humanoid-from-above: hair only.
#
# --- HAIR recipe, APPLIED (ref assets/sprites/ref/fur/durer_young_hare + skill 2d.md) ---
# Hair = MASS + VALUE + a FEW strands, never a clean disc. The canonical recipe (reuse for any
# haired humanoid), as built on the head below: (1) the head is a RADIAL GRADIENT, lit crown ->
# shadow nape; (2) a few lighter SHEEN strands fan from the crown whorl; (3) a few strays break
# the edge (a hard outline reads as a helmet/wig); (4) a dark parting between clumps. Kept to
# ~8 marks — the most-seen sprite must stay clean.
# Source for assets/sprites/player.png.
size 256x256
Background transparent

# the cloak — an A-line falling from the shoulder line: modest widening, curved hem,
# and a GRADIENT down the fall (lit at the shoulders, shadow at the hem — the drop reads)
name cloak
Poly (0.345,0.40) (0.655,0.40) (0.705,0.60)~ (0.66,0.775) (0.50,0.815)~ (0.34,0.775) (0.295,0.60)~ grad=60,86,138>24,34,60 dir=0.5,0.40,0.5,0.82

# arms — in scale with the body, emerging from under the shoulder line
name armL
Poly (0.405,0.405)@13 (0.345,0.315)@10 stroke=96,70,44
name armR
Poly (0.595,0.405)@13 (0.655,0.315)@10 stroke=96,70,44
name handL
Circle (0.336,0.295) r=0.028 rgb=190,152,118
name handR
Circle (0.664,0.295) r=0.028 rgb=190,152,118

# the shield — strapped over the LEFT forearm/hand (steel rim, wooden boss)
name shield
Circle (0.325,0.315) r=0.105 rgb=140,144,152
Circle (0.325,0.315) r=0.078 rgb=110,80,48
Circle (0.325,0.315) r=0.026 rgb=140,144,152

# the sword — from the right hand, angled forward (steel + guard)
name blade
Poly (0.655,0.285) (0.685,0.275) (0.745,0.095) (0.712,0.085) rgb=188,192,202
name guard
Line (0.630,0.270) - (0.700,0.300) w=5

# pauldrons — steel caps at the shoulder roots (the arms visibly attach under them)
name pauldrons
Circle (0.405,0.395) r=0.062 rgb=128,132,142
Circle (0.595,0.395) r=0.062 rgb=128,132,142

# the head — hair from above (no face). MASS = radial-gradient scalp (lit crown -> shadow
# nape); lighter SHEEN strands fan back from the crown whorl, a dark parting between them,
# and a few strays break the silhouette (a clean disc reads as a helmet). Hair recipe.
name head
Circle (0.50,0.345) r=0.075 radial=98,66,42>54,34,20 at=0.50,0.325,0.086
name parting
Poly (0.50,0.312)@2 (0.492,0.40)~@1 stroke=46,30,18
name sheen
Poly (0.50,0.325)@3 (0.50,0.405)~@1 stroke=124,88,56
Poly (0.486,0.325)@3 (0.451,0.392)~@1 stroke=116,82,52
Poly (0.514,0.325)@3 (0.549,0.392)~@1 stroke=116,82,52
name strays
Poly (0.466,0.398)@1.5 (0.449,0.430)~@0.6 stroke=120,86,56
Poly (0.534,0.398)@1.5 (0.551,0.430)~@0.6 stroke=120,86,56
Poly (0.50,0.414)@1.5 (0.50,0.446)~@0.6 stroke=110,80,52
